// ★ THE PROGRAM NOTHING WAS COMPILING.
//
// Every other TypeScript in this repo is typechecked by something:
//
//   packages/*                      `npm run build` runs tsc per package
//   deploy/mcp-relay/*.ts           relay-tests.yml — `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`
//   deploy/mcp-relay/tests/**       relay-tests.yml — `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.tests.json`
//                                   (that second program did not exist; this line claimed
//                                    the relay was covered while every relay test file was
//                                    in no program at all — see
//                                    deploy/mcp-relay/tsconfig.tests.json)
//   applications/*/bridge + src     bridge-typecheck.yml, via each bridge tsconfig's
//                                   `"../src/**/*.ts"` include
//   mcp-server, examples/*          bridge-typecheck.yml
//
// Two things were in none of them: `tests/**`, and `applications/shared-workspace/**` — the
// one application with no `bridge/` directory and therefore no tsconfig reaching its source.
// vitest transpiles with esbuild and does not typecheck, so `npx vitest run tests/` compiled
// nothing: it stripped the types and ran the JavaScript underneath.
//
// ★ MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. Deleting a required bail-out from `readAcceptanceRecord` — the
// branch that stops an acceptance naming no member from becoming a row with an empty
// `member` string — left all 237 tests GREEN. `tsc` catches it outright: the reader's
// `{iri} | {why}` union makes the branch structurally necessary. The suite said nothing
// because there was no compiler in the loop, and the missing behaviour test was found only
// by mutating the source by hand.
//
// This config is that compiler. `vitest.config.ts` runs it in `globalSetup`, so
// `npx vitest run tests/` cannot report green over source that does not compile — however
// vitest is invoked, and without depending on anyone remembering an npm script. CI runs it
// as its own named step too (bridge-typecheck.yml), because a gate whose only home is a
// setup hook is a gate one `--no-isolate` flag away from being skipped.
//
// `noEmit` and no `rootDir`: this program exists to be checked and never to be built.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false,
    // Tests destructure more than they use and bind fixtures they only pass along. Unused
    // locals are a style question; the defects this file exists to catch are type errors, and
    // failing the whole program on an unused `const` would get the gate turned off.
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noUnusedParameters": false,
    // The foxxi dashboard is React, and `foxxi-content-intelligence/src/learning-engineering.ts`
    // (reached from that vertical's tests) imports `dashboard-app/src/types.js`, which in turn
    // names a type out of `hypermedia.tsx`. With no `jsx` setting tsc refuses the `.tsx` on
    // sight — TS6142, an error about this program's configuration rather than about anything in
    // the source. `react-jsx` is what both the dashboard's own tsconfig and the bridge tsconfig
    // that already compiles this file use, so the setting here matches how it actually builds.
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  // ★ THE SAME GLOBS `vitest.config.ts` RUNS, plus the application source those tests import.
  // If vitest can execute it, this must be able to compile it — that identity is the whole
  // point, and a divergence between the two lists reopens the gap.
  //
  // It HAD diverged, and the comment here asserted the identity anyway. The list was
  // `tests/**` and `applications/shared-workspace/**`; vitest's `include` also names
  // `applications/**/tests/**`, `integrations/**/tests/**` and `mcp-server/tests/**`. That is
  // 66 of the 185 files vitest executes — a third of the suite — running with no compiler
  // behind them, under a comment warning that exactly this reopens the gap. Adding the three
  // missing globs surfaced 93 further errors in 27 files, all pre-existing, none new. They
  // were pinned first and then worked through: 4 remain, all in `tests/abac.test.ts`, and
  // `tools/typecheck-gate.mjs` records what the other 93 turned out to be — including six that
  // put `prov:wasAttributedTo <undefined>` in every compliance descriptor one bridge emitted.
  "include": [
    "tests/**/*.ts",
    "applications/shared-workspace/**/*.ts",
    "applications/**/tests/**/*.ts",
    "integrations/**/tests/**/*.ts",
    "mcp-server/tests/**/*.ts",
    // ★ THE SECURITY GUARDS THAT WERE IN NO TSC PROGRAM AT ALL.
    //
    // `applications/*/checks/**` holds the credential-issuer-binding, evidence-pointers and
    // statement-pagination guards. They are not matched by the `tests/**` globs above, and
    // not by any bridge tsconfig either — those include `../src/**/*.ts`, and `checks/` is a
    // SIBLING of `src/`, not a child. CI runs them with `npx tsx`, which strips types.
    //
    // Measured: appending `const _probe: number = "not a number";` to
    // `foxxi-content-intelligence/checks/credential-issuer-binding.check.ts` left
    // `tools/typecheck-gate.mjs`, every bridge tsc, and the lint gate ALL exit 0. A type
    // error in the guard that checks credential forgery merged green.
    "applications/**/checks/**/*.ts",
    // ★ AMBIENT DECLARATIONS. Nothing imports these, so they reach a program by inclusion or
    // not at all — and the globs above only name `.ts` under `tests/`. Each vertical's own
    // bridge tsconfig picks them up incidentally (its `../src/**/*.ts` matches `.d.ts` too),
    // which is why they existed and still went missing here:
    //
    //   vite-env.d.ts — `foxxi-content-intelligence/src/learning-engineering.ts` drags in the
    //     dashboard's `types.ts`, which drags in `hypermedia.tsx`, which reads
    //     `import.meta.env`. The declaration giving `ImportMeta` an `env` lives here.
    //   */types/*.d.ts — `applications/_shared/vc-jwt/types/` already declares
    //     `@digitalbazaar/bbs-signatures` (untyped upstream, no DefinitelyTyped stub) and
    //     `rdf-canonize`. Without them `bbs-2023.ts` reports TS7016 and the whole BBS+
    //     selective-disclosure surface degrades to `any` — a missing file, not missing types.
    "applications/**/vite-env.d.ts",
    "applications/**/types/*.d.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "**/dist/**", "scratchpad/**"]
}
